  "body": "## What changed\nThe Gate map headers of `crates/app/tests/grblhal_post.rs` and `crates/app/tests/tinyg_post.rs` named `app::post`, a module that now lives in `camcraft_post`. `no_gate_map_names_a_moved_module_as_app` rejects that, so `cargo test -p xtask` was red on main. Both headers now name `camcraft_post::post` and `camcraft_post::machine`; the rest of each header is unchanged. Comment-only change; no code or process files touched, so no `PROCESS_VERSION` bump.\n\n## Why the tests stay in `crates/app/tests/`\nAGENTS.md \"A test lives with the code it tests\" moves a suite to the owning crate only when it uses nothing from `crates/app/src`. Both suites import `camcraft_app::machine::parse_mch` (and the `app::posting` registry), so they stay in app. No follow-up issue was needed.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 91 passed, 0 failed (includes `no_gate_map_names_a_moved_module_as_app`, which was the red test).\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No app build or app test binary was run: the change is comment-only in two test files, and the header text is not compiled.\n- The quick-gate selection of the two suites is not re-measured; the xtask gate-map tests that cover selection pass.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only)\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #1331\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
